Thu Nov 12 23:31:10 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Add two more tests for skipping to skip-failing-curses-tests.patch

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 23:29:45 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Update to Python 3.16.0a2:
  - Security
    - CVE 2026-115791, gh-161705: Remove sys.path[0] in gzip,
      tarfile and zipfile command line interface to prevent
      shadowing standard library modules from extracted files.
      Issue reported by Jelle Zijlstra, patch by Gregory P. Smith
      and Victor Stinner.
    - CVE 2026-124249, gh-161569: Fix http.cookiejar.CookieJar
      deleting a stored cookie when a response from an unrelated
      host sets an already expired cookie with a Domain or Path
      attribute pointing at that cookie. The cookie policy is now
      consulted before an expired cookie is allowed to delete an
      existing one.
    - CVE 2026-19552, gh-161503: ssl.get_server_certificate() now
      verifies that the server hostname matches its certificate
      when the caller specifies ca_certs.
    - gh-161192: Update bundled libexpat to version 2.10.0 for
      the fixes to CVE 2026-113351, CVE 2026-115506, CVE
      2026-117610 and CVE 2026-118370.
    - CVE 2026-116566, gh-160898: socket.getaddrinfo() now
      rejects null bytes within host and port parameters as this
      previously caused the values to be silently truncated.
      (bsc#1289106)
    - CVE 2026-115559, gh-160369: imaplib.IMAP4.starttls() now
      rejects unexpected plaintext buffered after the STARTTLS
      response, preventing it from being processed as
      TLS-protected data.
    - gh-160279: Prevent venv from importing modules from the
      root of an existing virtual environment when installing or
      upgrading pip.
    - gh-160499: Fix unbounded memory growth in asyncio TLS
      connections when a peer stops reading but keeps sending
      records that make OpenSSL generate its own replies (such as
      TLS 1.2 renegotiation alerts). Reading from the peer is now
      paused when this output accumulates, instead of only when
      application data does.
    - gh-160506: Fix os.path.realpath() on Windows returning the
      wrong path for a broken relative symbolic link reached
      through a symbolic link to a directory. This allowed
      tarfile extraction with the 'data' or 'tar' filter to
      create a file outside the destination directory.
    - gh-161323: On Windows, the 'tar' and 'data' tarfile
      extraction filters now refuse member names and link targets
      that have a drive but are not absolute, such as C:foo, with
      AbsolutePathError or AbsoluteLinkError. Such members could
      be extracted outside the destination directory. Fixes CVE
      2026-107784.
    - gh-160420: Fix zoneinfo.ZoneInfo on Windows accepting keys
      in which a component after a / starts with a drive letter,
      such as America/C:\file. Such a key could open a file
      outside the tzdata package; it now raises ValueError.
    - gh-160300: Fix http.cookiejar.DefaultCookiePolicy accepting
      and returning cookies with a negative Version attribute
      without checking their domain against the request host.
      Such cookies are now ignored.
    - CVE 2026-114583, gh-160097: tarfile.tar_filter() now
      rejects link members whose path resolves to the destination
      directory itself, as tarfile.data_filter() already did.
      (bsc#1288258)
    - CVE 2026-115557, gh-160040: ssl now rejects TLS certificate
      chains that contain any of a set of compromised eMudhra
      intermediate CA keys. This is an extraordinary measure and
      a last line of defense: removing trust is primarily the job
      of the platform root store, and the built-in denylist only
      blocks connections while that update has not yet reached
      the OS, a container image, or a bundled trust store in
      various Python packages. Entries are added to the denylist
      only under a very high threshold. The denylist matches on
      the public key (the SHA-256 digest of the RFC 5280
      SubjectPublicKeyInfo), so it also covers the cross-signed
      certificates that reuse one of the distrusted keys.
      (bsc#1287903)
    - gh-159894: Bump the version of pip bundled in ensurepip to
      version 26.2.2.
    - gh-159428: mimetypes no longer reads the files listed in
      mimetypes.knownfiles by default on Windows, and uses only
      the registry.
    - gh-158928: Fix a buffer overflow when initializing a
      bytearray from an iterator.
    - gh-157953: Update bundled libexpat to version 2.9.0.
  - Core and Builtins
    - gh-160267: Fix a crash when profiling.sampling profiles a
      process that creates and destroys threads or
      subinterpreters quickly. Memory of deleted thread and
      interpreter states is now reused for new states instead of
      being freed until the runtime is finalized.
    - gh-161420: Restore mimalloc’s previous behavior of
      processing delayed frees from other threads on every
      generic malloc call, reverting the change introduced in
      v2.2.2.
    - gh-161242: Speed up AttributeError, ImportError and
      NameError by enabling The Vectorcall Protocol. Unexpected
      keyword arguments are now reported by name.
    - gh-161433: Add context notes to TypeError raised while
      hashing a tuple, identifying the index of the item whose
      hash failed.
    - gh-129724: Fix the marshal output of compiled code, and so
      .pyc files, differing for the same source depending on what
      ran before in the process. This affected private names in
      classes with non-ASCII names, and compile() of an AST with
      names not created by ast.parse().
    - gh-161366: Fix a deadlock in the garbage collector of the
      free-threaded build when gc.DEBUG_COLLECTABLE is set and
      another thread is writing to sys.stderr. The debug output
      is now written after the other threads are resumed.
    - gh-161419: Fix a crash in the free-threaded build where a
      weak reference could revive an object whose finalizer had
      already run during deallocation, causing it to be
      deallocated twice.
    - gh-161288: Fix a crash in the perf trampoline (-X perf) on
      builds with clang’s -fsanitize=function, which
      -fsanitize=undefined enables since clang 17.
    - gh-159184: Fix a leak of NaN constants in code objects
      created by marshal.loads() on the free-threaded build.
    - gh-161229: __lazy_import__() now treats None for globals
      and locals the same as omitting them, matching its
      signature.
    - gh-160872: Optimize division and remainder operations on
      large int values.
    - gh-160773: Fix a crash in str() of an OSError when
      formatting one of its attributes modifies the others.
    - gh-160682: Fix a bug in the free-threaded build where
      garbage collection could prematurely collect the function
      object of a running method.
    - gh-153568: Speed up ast.parse() by ~15.8% and reduce the
      memory used by ~51.6% by storing node attributes as inline
      values instead of in a per-node dictionary.
    - gh-160491: Fix the location reported for invalid escape
      sequences in f-strings and t-strings. The SyntaxError now
      points at the literal part that contains the escape,
      instead of at the closing quote.
    - gh-160050: Use asymptotically faster divmod()
      implementation for integer modulo of large integers.
    - gh-160268: Fix a crash in tokenize when a mismatched
      closing bracket follows the opening brace of an f-string or
      t-string replacement field, as in f'{]a'. It now raises the
      same “unmatched” error as the parser.
    - gh-160245: Reduce the size of parser memo entries on 64-bit
      platforms by reordering fields to remove padding. Patch by
      Shamil Abdulaev.
    - gh-106045: Fix venv path discovery when the base executable
      resolves to a location outside the installation pointed to
      by the home key in pyvenv.cfg. The standard library is now
      found from home, and extension modules from the resolved
      executable’s installation, instead of falling back to the
      compiled-in prefix.
    - gh-160162: Fix a crash on 32-bit platforms when left
      shifting an int by a count close to sys.maxsize *
      sys.int_info.bits_per_digit. OverflowError is now raised,
      as for other too large counts.
    - gh-160179: Fix bytearray.__init__() leaving uninitialized
      memory in the object when it fails on a list or tuple
      containing an integer not in range(256). The object is now
      empty after the failed call.
    - gh-160132: Reduce memory usage during compilation by
      reordering the fields of the internal basic block structure
      to reduce padding. Patch by Shamil Abdulaev.
    - gh-159739: Raise MemoryError instead of returning an
      incorrect result if round() runs out of memory while
      rounding a float.
    - gh-159739: Fix a possible crash when assigning metadata to
      classmethod or staticmethod objects.
    - gh-159739: Fix a race in list.__sizeof__() when a list is
      concurrently resized on a free-threaded build.
    - gh-159739: Fix a reference leak when the value of a type
      alias is evaluated recursively or concurrently.
    - gh-159739: Fix a crash in free-threaded builds when
      codecs.unregister() is called concurrently.
    - gh-160368: On Linux, allow timed semaphore waits to use the
      monotonic clock when sem_clockwait is available at runtime,
      even if Python was built with older libc headers.
    - gh-159493: Superinstructions are now formed after the
      compiler decides which LOAD_FAST instructions can borrow
      their reference. This fixes reference count contention
      slowdown on the free-threaded build for single-line loops
      and comprehensions.
    - gh-159963: Fix a regression in Python 3.15.0 where threads
      importing submodules of packages for the first time could
      raise _DeadlockError or a spurious “partially initialized
      module” ImportError, or block one another, with no circular
      import involved. importlib.import_module() now returns the
      partially initialized module in a cross-thread circular
      import, as the import statement does, instead of raising
      _DeadlockError.
    - gh-159101: Fix use-after-free when __del__() changes the
      base class. Patch by Sergey Miryanov.
    - gh-158195: Fix a deadlock in the free-threaded build
      between a thread that stops the world while running Python
      code under the type lock (for example a custom metaclass
      mro() or the __eq__ of a str subclass used as a class
      __dict__ key) and a thread that assigns to a special method
      or to __bases__ of a class. The type lock is no longer held
      while waiting for a stop-the-world; the prepared slot, MRO
      and bases updates are validated with the world stopped and
      recomputed if they went stale.
    - gh-159739: Fix reference leaks when free-threaded garbage
      collection aborts early because of an allocation error.
    - gh-159739: Prevent free-threaded builds from interning and
      immortalizing complex subclasses in code object constants.
    - gh-159739: Fix a reference leak in binary, ternary, and
      comparison operations on weak reference proxies when
      another operand is a dead proxy.
    - gh-159739: Fix a crash when constructing an error for
      invalid generic alias arguments.
    - gh-159739: Allow the garbage collector to break reference
      cycles involving property accessors or names.
    - gh-159860: Fix false sharing between the per-thread QSBR
      states in the free-threaded build on AArch64 CPUs with
      128-byte cache lines, such as Apple Silicon. CPU-bound
      threads that share no objects now scale like processes
      there.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash if allocation fails while creating
      a string.templatelib.Template iterator.
    - gh-159739: Propagate errors during generic class
      construction and avoid a crash after failed generic alias
      substitution.
    - gh-159739: Raise OverflowError when the absolute value of a
      dynamic printf-style formatting width is too large.
    - gh-159739: Fix a reference leak in gc.get_objects() and
      gc.get_referrers() when an internal allocation fails in the
      free-threaded build.
    - gh-159739: Fix a crash in warnings.warn() when
      skip_file_prefixes is an empty tuple subclass. Propagate
      allocation errors when creating the fallback filename.
    - gh-159739: Fix memory leaks during interpreter startup when
      a path configuration file is empty or too large, or when an
      audit hook rejects a command.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash when an interpreter configuration
      string cannot be encoded as UTF-8.
    - gh-159739: Preserve the original SyntaxError if allocating
      optional error metadata fails.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash if formatting an integer with the
      c presentation type runs out of memory.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash when a module filename cannot be
      encoded as UTF-8.
    - gh-159813: Add a fast path for None in
      PyUnicodeWriter_WriteRepr(). Patch by Donghee Na.
    - gh-159652: Fix a hang when an import fails with
      RecursionError because the C stack is nearly exhausted:
      releasing the import locks could itself fail and leave the
      global import lock or a module lock held forever, so that
      later imports in other threads blocked indefinitely. The
      import system now raises RecursionError before taking an
      import lock when there is not enough stack left to release
      it.
    - gh-159603: On FreeBSD, call pthread_attr_get_np() to get
      the stack size (and guard size) of the current thread.
      Patch by Victor Stinner.
    - gh-159564: Improve the performance and thread scaling of
      dereferencing weak references in the free-threaded build.
      Dereferencing a weak reference no longer takes a lock.
    - gh-87613: Speed up calling slice by adding a vectorcall
      implementation of the constructor generated by Argument
      Clinic. Patch by Pieter Eendebak.
    - gh-130279: Fix bug where compiler did not set the right
      exception handler for some jump instructions.
    - gh-87613: Speed up creating weakref.ref objects by adding a
      vectorcall implementation of the constructor generated by
      Argument Clinic. Patch by Pieter Eendebak.
    - gh-159449: Fix a free-threaded asyncio race leading to
      segfaults.
    - gh-132042: Speed up class creation by resolving the special
      method slots of a new class with one pass over each class
      dict along the MRO instead of one lookup per slot name and
      per class.
    - gh-159434: Fix reading a function’s __annotations__ using
      borrowed references to __annotate__ and the internal
      annotations tuple while running code that can replace them.
      If __annotations__ is set while __annotate__ runs, the
      newly set value is now kept.
    - gh-159431: Fix an assertion failure, or an immortal object
      becoming mortal, on the free threaded build when an object
      passed to the internal delayed decref mechanism is immortal
      or becomes immortal before the delayed decref is processed
      by the garbage collector.
    - gh-159430: Report the correct exception if looking up
      __bytes__() raises an exception while performing
      %-formatting of bytes.
    - gh-159399: Fix a crash in codecs.encode() and
      codecs.decode() in the free-threaded build when another
      thread concurrently unregisters a codec search function.
      Patch by Christian Aurich Zanettini Martins.
    - gh-159320: Add dynamic detection of stack sizes on Android,
      allowing safer deep recursion.
    - gh-159294: Fix a crash in a debug build when creating an
      ExceptionGroup or BaseExceptionGroup fails with
      MemoryError. Patch by Christian Aurich Zanettini Martins.
    - gh-159288: Fix a crash when walking a very long chain of
      lazy import placeholders, as created by an aliased dotted
      import such as lazy import a.b.c as d. RecursionError is
      now raised instead.
    - gh-159136: Setting __name__, __qualname__, __doc__ or
      __module__ on a function no longer stops all threads in the
      free-threaded build. The setters now use the per-object
      lock and defer freeing the old value with QSBR, the same
      approach used for generator __name__. This fixes a large
      slowdown in multi-threaded code using functools.wraps()
      since 3.14.7. Readers of these attributes now use atomic
      loads, and argument error reporting reads __qualname__
      after keyword comparisons, which may execute Python code
      and replace it. Previously this could use a freed object.
    - gh-159244: Fix a crash in dict and dict.update() in the
      free-threaded build when another thread concurrently
      mutates a list used as a key/value pair. Patch by Christian
      Aurich Zanettini Martins.
    - gh-68241: Add EXIT_FAILURE and EXIT_SUCCESS in the sys
      module.
    - gh-159188: In the free-threaded build, compile() no longer
      immortalizes the constants of the code objects when it is
      given an AST object, as was already the case for a source
      string. The output of marshal for such code no longer
      depends on the code objects which were created before in
      the process.
    - gh-159111: Update mimalloc version from 2.1.2 to 2.5.2.
      Patch by Donghee Na.
    - gh-159041: Fix a use-after-free in asyncio task bookkeeping
      when a finalizer creates a task during thread shutdown.
    - gh-158973: Reset the warnings lock in the child after
      os.fork(), before clearing other threads’ states, to avoid
      deadlocks when their finalizers issue warnings. Preserve
      the lock’s recursion depth if the forking thread owns it.
    - gh-87613: Speed up bytes and bytearray construction by
      adding The Vectorcall Protocol support.
    - gh-158816: Speed up deleting items from split dictionaries
      (for example the materialized __dict__ of an instance with
      inline values) by skipping a redundant hash table probe.
    - gh-158197: Fix crashes and debug-build assertion failures
      in the free-threaded build when iterating over a split
      dictionary while another thread deletes entries or clears
      it. Publish insertion-order updates atomically so readers
      cannot observe an increased size before the corresponding
      order entry is initialized.
    - gh-158525: Fix slow dict.copy() for dicts with many deleted
      entries in the free-threaded build.
    - gh-158529: Fixed crash on Android x86_64, API levels 27-28,
      caused by mimalloc calling system calls directly.
    - gh-158121: Fix missing sys.monitoring INSTRUCTION events
      when a LINE callback returns sys.monitoring.DISABLE.
    - gh-158304: Speed up iteration over asynchronous generators:
      values yielded to async for no longer create and discard a
      StopIteration exception at every nesting level. The
      async_generators pyperformance benchmark is about 30%
      faster. Patch by Shamil Abdulaev.
    - gh-157746: Reduce the overhead of PyErr_CheckSignals() when
      no signal is pending: the cheap flag checks are now done
      before the main-thread check and the remote debugger
      configuration lookup.
    - gh-132414: Quote the invalid option in the error message
      for an unknown command-line option: Invalid option '-z'
      instead of Unknown option: -z. A stray space, as passed by
      a shebang line like #!/usr/bin/python3 -q -i, is now
      reported as Invalid option '- '.
    - gh-157361: Implement aiter() in Python instead of C, in the
      frozen _pybuiltins module. The async iterator returned by
      aiter(callable, ...) now has a plain coroutine __anext__(),
      so introspection tools such as asyncio.print_call_graph()
      can see through it into the awaited callable result.
    - gh-157194: Fix a data race in the free-threaded build,
      reported by ThreadSanitizer, between the specializer
      reading an instruction opcode and another thread writing
      it. Only reachable when thread-local bytecode is disabled
      with -X tlbc=0, which makes threads share one copy of the
      bytecode.
    - gh-156443: Speed up float() conversion and true division of
      large int values.
    - gh-135385: Reduce the memory consumption of instances of
      classes which define __slots__ and also have a __dict__.
      Space for the attributes stored in slots is no longer
      reserved in the inline values of every instance.
    - gh-106045: Fix standard library discovery in virtual
      environments created from a Python executable symlink
      located outside its base installation.
    - gh-156399: Fix a regression where attribute access on a
      types.ModuleType subclass could bypass a data descriptor
      defined on the subclass. The LOAD_ATTR_MODULE
      specialization guarded on tp_getattro, which subclasses
      inherit, and then read the module dictionary directly.
    - gh-127716: On the free-threaded build, memoryview lifetime
      and bookkeeping operations are now thread safe: an
      operation that reads the buffer holds the managed buffer
      for its duration, so a concurrent release() can no longer
      free the buffer under it; slicing a memoryview from several
      threads no longer loses buffer registrations and raises
      ValueError: operation forbidden on released memoryview
      object; and hash() of a memoryview is no longer a data
      race. As a result release() may now return while an
      operation started by another thread is still running, see
      Thread safety for memoryview objects.
    - gh-154318: Fix a crash when hashing a deeply nested tuple
      or frozendict. A RecursionError is now raised instead of
      overflowing the C stack.
    - gh-153568: Speed up parsing of simple expressions by
      recognizing single-token atoms without descending the full
      precedence rule chain.
    - gh-153014: Fix a data race on the garbage collector debug
      flag in free-threading builds: gc.set_debug() and
      gc.get_debug() now access it atomically.
    - gh-152631: Fix ast.parse() ability to parse lazy imports
      with feature_version older than 3.15, now it properly
      raises SyntaxError.
    - gh-149816: Fix a race in free-threaded builds where storing
      an instance attribute could use a stale borrowed reference
      to an instance __dict__ after another thread replaced it.
    - gh-151818: Fix a double-free crash in list.append() (the
      specialized CALL_LIST_APPEND instruction) when growing the
      list fails with MemoryError.
    - gh-151060: Fix a crash or memory corruption in sum() when
      summing a float subclass instance into a complex running
      total.
    - gh-150075: tar.addfile() now sets member offsets in TarInfo
      objects
    - gh-148891: Fix a crash in contextvars.Context.run() where a
      GC invocation could free the current HAMT during traverse.
    - gh-69605: Fix REPL completions inserted incorrectly when
      there was spaces in import statements.
    - gh-69605: Insert import after from x.y.z <tab> in the REPL
      auto-completion.
    - gh-145019: Improve SyntaxError when match alternative
      patterns bind different names. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-137966: Add support for additional special names to the
      built-in help() function. Patch by Adam Hartz.
    - gh-125873: Improved error message when an environment
      variable is misconfigured.
    - gh-122901: Speed up creating str objects from non-ASCII
      character data.
    - gh-116477: Speed up the range object constructor in the
      case of a single argument.
  - Library
    - gh-161475: Fix ctypes structures containing arrays of
      floating-point type returned by value on 64-bit Linux
      SPARC.
    - gh-71199: Change os module types such as DirEntry to report
      os as their module on every platform. Pickled objects using
      the platform-specific qualified name, such as
      nt.times_result, still load.
    - gh-142782: Fix a use-after-free in zoneinfo.ZoneInfo when a
      key’s __eq__ clears the cache during a lookup. Strong cache
      keys are now compared by string contents.
    - gh-161415: Remove FILES and unicode from the related help
      topics listed by help() for the TYPES and UNICODE topics.
      Neither exists in Python 3, so asking for help on them
      failed.
    - gh-161414: Remove the backquote from the symbols listed by
      help(), asking for help on it reported that no
      documentation was found.
    - gh-161389: Fixes a crash in decimal.Context when passing
      invalid signaling dicts as flags and traps.
    - gh-161387: Fix a crash in decimal when the internal
      decimal_context contextvars.ContextVar holds a value that
      is not a context.
    - gh-161295: reprlib.Repr objects now have a meaningful
      __repr__() describing the instance attributes.
    - gh-161259: Improved the accuracy of
      statistics.correlation() for very small inputs, where the
      product of the sums of squares is subnormal rather than
      zero.
    - gh-93821: Fix asyncio.ProactorEventLoop servers that
      stopped accepting new connections on Windows when a client
      reset its connection before it was accepted (WinError 64,
      ERROR_NETNAME_DELETED). The listening socket is now kept
      open and the server continues to accept connections.
    - gh-161076: Fix asyncio leaving a half-created transport
      registered with the event loop and the server when setting
      TCP_NODELAY on a socket fails. Such a failure could make
      asyncio.Server.wait_closed() hang and prevent new
      connections from being served. Errors from
      setsockopt(TCP_NODELAY) are now ignored.
    - gh-161233: Fix unraisable TypeError when None was passed as
      a timer to cProfile.Profile.
    - gh-161212: Bump the version of pip bundled in ensurepip to
      version 26.3.
    - gh-161178: Fix asyncio.Task.print_stack() to include frames
      from async generator operations. Patch by Timofei Ivankov
    - gh-161179: Fix the function names in the error messages of
      os.spawnve(), os.preadv() and tkinter.Wm.wm_attributes().
    - gh-161166: Fix asyncio.Task.print_stack() displaying an
      incorrect exception line after a finally block. Patch by
      Timofei Ivankov.
    - gh-161124: Fix asyncio.print_call_graph() reporting event
      loop frames when depth exceeds the task stack. Patch by
      Timofei Ivankov.
    - gh-161083: Fix stale task nodes left by asyncio.gather()
      when argument validation fails. Patch by Timofei Ivankov
    - gh-161039: Fix the pydoc pager not detecting less 706 and
      newer.
    - gh-137549: asyncio.timeout() now inserts TimeoutError into
      the context chain of sub-exceptions of a
      BaseExceptionGroup, as it already did for ExceptionGroup.
    - gh-160782: venv: a symbolic link or junction in place of a
      directory inside the environment now raises ValueError
      instead of being followed.
    - gh-160782: venv: a backslash before a quote in the prompt
      or the path no longer breaks activate.fish.
    - gh-160429: Fix asyncio.ProactorEventLoop socket transports
      leaving the socket open, and asyncio.Server.wait_closed()
      hanging, when the peer resets the connection while the
      transport is being closed.
    - gh-160929: Fix reverse union with ChainMap to preserve its
      lookup semantics for defaulting mappings such as Counter
      and defaultdict.
    - gh-50720: urllib.error.URLError now sets the errno and
      strerror attributes from reason when it is an OSError. On
      Windows, winerror is set as well.
    - gh-53089: urllib.request.HTTPDigestAuthHandler now sends
      uri="/" in the Digest Authorization header for URLs with an
      empty path, such as http://example.com, matching the
      request-target sent by http.client. Previously it sent
      uri="", which servers could reject. Patch by Senthil
      Kumaran.
    - gh-109564: Fix a race in asyncio where closing a server
      after it accepted a connection, but before the connection’s
      transport was created, reported an AssertionError to the
      exception handler. Such connections are now closed quietly.
    - gh-66333: Allow Ctrl-C to interrupt execution resumed with
      the pdb next, until, and return commands without unwinding
      the debugged program, as with continue.
    - gh-59515: urllib.request.HTTPDigestAuthHandler and
      urllib.request.ProxyDigestAuthHandler now parse all
      WWW-Authenticate (or Proxy-Authenticate) headers and accept
      multiple challenges per header: the first Digest challenge
      is used.
    - gh-53852: urllib.request.ProxyDigestAuthHandler now raises
      HTTPError with status code 407 (Proxy Authentication
      Required) instead of 401 when proxy authentication fails.
    - gh-160811: Fix io.TextIOWrapper.tell() reading past the end
      of the buffer after seek().
    - gh-160806: Fix the pure-Python implementation of
      datetime.timedelta losing sub-second precision with large
      float arguments. It now gives the same results as the C
      implementation.
    - gh-160804: asyncio call graph introspection now includes
      frames of generator based awaitables, such as generators
      returned by __await__ and types.coroutine() generators.
    - gh-160781: Fix io.BytesIO implementation of
      io.IOBase.truncate() rejecting sizes larger than 2**31 - 1
      on Windows.
    - gh-160781: Fix io.StringIO implementation of
      io.IOBase.truncate() rejecting sizes larger than 2**31 - 1
      on Windows.
    - gh-160781: Fix io.BytesIO raising SystemError instead of
      OverflowError when writing at a position close to
      sys.maxsize.
    - gh-158500: datetime.date.fromisoformat() now rejects
      strings with trailing characters after a basic-format date,
      such as '2020010112'. The pure-Python
      datetime.datetime.fromisoformat() now rejects a date
      followed by a bare separator, such as '2020-01-01T',
      matching the C implementation.
    - gh-160708: Fix out-of-bounds memory access in bool() on
      ctypes simple objects enlarged by ctypes.resize(), and when
      passing such objects to a foreign function.
    - gh-160427: Fix buffer of a detached io.TextIOWrapper
      raising ValueError instead of returning None.
    - gh-160596: Fix the error message for invalid data passed to
      asyncio.proactor_events.sendto().
    - gh-160561: Fix a descriptor leak in socket.fromfd() when
      the socket constructor rejects its arguments. The
      duplicated descriptor was never closed.
    - gh-160433: Fix incorrect backup names around daylight
      saving time changes in
      logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler, including
      delayed rollovers.
    - gh-160549: Fix a crash when a
      compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor that uses worker threads
      and a ZstdDict is deallocated, or the interpreter exits,
      while data passed to compress() is still being compressed.
    - gh-160535: Fix a crash in compression.zstd when the garbage
      collector frees a ZstdCompressor that uses worker threads
      together with its ZstdDict before the compression of
      already submitted data has finished.
    - gh-60299: Fix urllib.request.ProxyDigestAuthHandler failing
      to authenticate. It looked up credentials using the target
      request URL instead of the proxy’s authority, so passwords
      registered via add_password() against the proxy never
      matched. Patch by Senthil Kumaran.
    - gh-160386: Applied changes to importlib.metadata from
      importlib_metadata 9.1: distribution discovery now prefers
      the greater of several metadata directories supplied by one
      path, so stale metadata left by an unclean upgrade no
      longer shadows the version in use; a missing required
      metadata field now raises a KeyError naming both the field
      and the distribution; EntryPoint value validation is
      deferred until the value is used, so one malformed entry
      point no longer prevents others from being selected;
      importlib.metadata.diagnose no longer crashes on a metadata
      directory with no metadata file or no declared name; and
      SimplePath.joinpath and SimplePath.__truediv__ take other
      positional-only.
    - gh-160520: Fix asyncio SSL transports not applying
      ssl_shutdown_timeout when the peer has sent EOF but does
      not read the data still queued for it. Closing such a
      connection could wait indefinitely; it is now aborted with
      TimeoutError once the timeout expires.
    - gh-160326: Raise ValueError for a NaN timeout in
      threading.Condition.wait() and the blocking calls built on
      it, such as threading.Event.wait(),
      threading.Semaphore.acquire() and queue.Queue.get(),
      instead of returning at once or looping without ever timing
      out.
    - gh-160314: Raise an error in lzma.LZMAFile,
      lzma.decompress(), bz2.BZ2File and bz2.decompress() for a
      damaged .xz or bzip2 stream that follows another stream,
      instead of silently ignoring it and everything after it as
      trailing data.
    - gh-159739: Fix crashes in sqlite3 when a row or text
      factory is replaced during a query, when cursor metadata is
      read during execution in a free-threaded build, or when
      allocating cursor metadata fails.
    - gh-159739: Fix crashes in profiling.tracing when a custom
      timer reinitializes the profiler or its result clears or
      disables the profiler during conversion or cleanup.
    - gh-159739: Fix crashes in xml.parsers.expat when a
      character data callback disables buffering or clears
      another handler during a flush, or when interning an
      attribute name changes ordered_attributes.
    - gh-159739: Fix the hz codec sometimes encoding ~ as a
      single ~ in text that mixes ASCII and Chinese characters,
      and the incremental iso2022_* codecs mishandling an escape
      sequence split across calls or keeping the previous
      character set after reset(). Also fix possible crashes in
      the CJK incremental and stream codecs when their errors
      attribute or their class’s codec attribute is replaced
      while they are in use.
    - gh-159739: Fix crashes in io.TextIOWrapper and
      io.IncrementalNewlineDecoder when a callback changes the
      active codec or decoded buffer. io.StringIO now raises
      ValueError if converting the size passed to truncate()
      closes the stream.
    - gh-160310: Fix quadratic time complexity of
      gzip.decompress(), bz2.decompress(), lzma.decompress() and
      compression.zstd.decompress() on data consisting of many
      concatenated members.
    - gh-160522: Fix the incremental encoders and stream writers
      of the stateful CJK codecs (iso2022_* and hz) keeping a
      changed shift state after an encode() or write() call
      failed. The next call could omit the escape sequence,
      writing multibyte characters in ASCII mode.
    - gh-160316: Fix re.Pattern.match(),
      re.Pattern.prefixmatch(), re.Pattern.fullmatch() and the
      match() and prefixmatch() methods of scanner objects
      returning an empty match, or reading past the end of the
      string, when pos is greater than endpos. They now return
      None, as documented.
    - gh-160324: Fix a crash or garbage data when an io.StringIO
      object is used again after one of its methods failed with
      MemoryError. The object now keeps its contents.
    - gh-160406: Fix in-place filtering in fileinput deleting the
      file when it cannot be opened or the output file cannot be
      created: the backup file is now kept. The output file is
      now created exclusively, so FileExistsError is raised if a
      file or symbolic link appears under the name of the input
      file.
    - gh-160513: Fix asyncio.loop.start_tls() and
      asyncio.StreamWriter.start_tls() not calling the protocol’s
      connection_lost() when the connection is lost, the
      handshake times out or the call is cancelled during the TLS
      handshake. asyncio.StreamWriter.wait_closed() no longer
      waits forever after such a failure.
    - gh-160297: Fix tarfile.TarFile.extractall() and
      tarfile.TarFile.extract() changing the mode, modification
      time and owner of a file outside the destination directory
      when a hard link member is extracted as a copy of a
      symbolic link member, for example with the 'tar' filter.
    - gh-161086: Fix the gzip command-line interface ignoring
      gzip --fast and gzip --best when compressing files given as
      arguments.
    - gh-161112: Fix shutil.make_archive() adding the zip archive
      being created to itself when it is written inside the
      directory being archived or a symbolic link in that
      directory refers to it.
    - gh-161088: Fix the gzip command-line interface writing
      through a symbolic link at the output file name. Like gzip,
      it now replaces an existing output file with a new one that
      has the permission bits of the input file.
    - gh-161094: Fix zipfile.is_zipfile() raising ValueError
      instead of returning False for a file-like object, such as
      io.BytesIO, whose end of central directory record places
      the central directory before the start of the file.
    - gh-161096: Fix zoneinfo.ZoneInfo.from_file() accepting TZif
      data with a negative or oversized abbreviation block, which
      could use hundreds of times the file size in memory; it now
      raises ValueError. Abbreviation indexes above 127 now also
      give the correct time zone abbreviation.
    - gh-161106: Fix plistlib.dump() and plistlib.dumps() with
      FMT_BINARY holding on to memory proportional to the size of
      large arrays and dictionaries after the call returns.
    - gh-161098: Fix multiprocessing.shared_memory.ShareableList
      leaving its newly created shared memory block behind when a
      value cannot be stored, such as an integer outside the
      signed 64-bit range.
    - gh-161108: Fix quadratic time complexity of clear() and
      popitem() on configparser.ConfigParser objects and their
      section proxies. Clearing a section no longer fails part
      way with InterpolationError on a value it removes.
    - gh-161110: Fix getElementById() in xml.dom.minidom so that
      it returns the first element in document order when several
      elements have the same ID. Previously, the result could
      differ between calls on an unmodified document.
    - gh-161100: Fix ipaddress.IPv6Interface.is_unspecified
      returning False for the IPv4-mapped address ::ffff:0.0.0.0.
      It now gives the same result as
      ipaddress.IPv6Address.is_unspecified.
    - gh-161102: Fix the incremental decoder of the idna codec
      decoding some dots twice when its input starts with empty
      labels, for example b".example.com". Reading a run of dots
      through io.TextIOWrapper no longer produces quadratically
      more text than the input holds.
    - gh-161092: Fix the uu codec decoder taking any line that
      starts with begin, such as beginning of the report, as the
      header of the encoded data. Like the email package, it now
      requires begin followed by an octal mode and skips other
      lines as leading text.
    - gh-161090: Fix the punycode codec accepting a delimiter (-)
      that is not preceded by any basic code point. Such input,
      for example b'-80a1acny', now raises UnicodeDecodeError, as
      required by RFC 3492.
    - gh-159739: Fix time functions returning a negative year or
      failing to accept their own output for large timestamps on
      platforms that support them. Avoid reporting an incorrect
      year in errors raised by datetime for those timestamps.
    - gh-159739: Fix a crash when a ctypes structure subclass
      cannot be created due to an allocation failure.
    - gh-159739: Fix clearing a pickle.Unpickler memo so that the
      unpickler can be reused for independent records.
    - gh-160171: On the server side,
      ssl.SSLSocket.get_unverified_chain() now returns the
      client’s certificate when the session was resumed from a
      session ticket, instead of an empty list, and returns an
      empty list instead of raising AttributeError when the
      client sent no certificate.
    - gh-160181: Fix io.BytesIO.getvalue() sometimes returning a
      bytes object with the hash of earlier contents after the
      buffer was written to, which made dict and set lookups with
      it fail.
    - gh-160187: Fix the ISO-2022 decoders (iso2022_jp,
      iso2022_kr and related) accepting escape sequences that
      designate a character set to the wrong code element (G0, G1
      or G2). Such sequences now raise UnicodeDecodeError instead
      of producing wrong text or RuntimeError.
    - gh-160185: Fix codecs.StreamWriter.reset() of the stateful
      CJK codecs (hz and the iso2022_* family) not writing the
      sequence that returns the output to ASCII. seek(0) of
      codecs.StreamWriter, codecs.StreamReaderWriter and
      codecs.StreamRecoder now resets the writer before moving
      the stream position.
    - gh-160176: Fix a crash in tkinter when a deeply nested or
      recursive list or tuple is passed to Tcl, or a deeply
      nested Tcl list is converted to Python. These now raise
      ValueError (beyond 1000 levels) and RecursionError
      respectively.
    - gh-159739: Fix a possible crash in abc.ABCMeta instance
      checks when a subclass-checking callback changes the
      instance’s class.
    - gh-159739: Fix the truncate method on io.BytesIO when
      converting its size argument closes the stream or exports
      its buffer.
    - gh-159739: Raise TypeError if a string subclass returns a
      non-string during newline translation in io.TextIOWrapper.
      Recheck the stream state if the replacement callback
      closes, detaches or reinitializes the stream.
    - gh-159739: Fix contextvars.ContextVar returning a stale
      value after a reentrant finalizer changes it during
      reset().
    - gh-159739: Detect recursive _as_parameter_ chains for
      ctypes calls without argument types.
    - gh-159739: Fix a possible crash when a list of sqlite3
      parameters is modified concurrently on a free-threaded
      build.
    - gh-160104: Synchronized zipfile.Path with zipp 4.1.2.
      zipfile.Path.iterdir() now raises NotADirectoryError
      instead of ValueError when the path does not reference a
      directory. Character classes in zipfile.Path.glob() and
      zipfile.Path.rglob() patterns now follow shell-style
      semantics, treating a leading ! as negation and ^ as a
      literal, and no longer match path separators.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash when a threading.local subclass
      finalizer accesses attributes after construction fails.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash when a queue.SimpleQueue subclass
      finalizer adds an item after construction fails.
    - gh-100609: str() of a zipfile.Path whose underlying zipfile
      has no filename, such as one constructed from an
      io.BytesIO, now renders that filename as :zipfile: instead
      of raising TypeError. The root of a zipfile is also no
      longer rendered with a trailing slash. Synchronized with
      zipp 3.23.1.
    - gh-89721: Add copy_dir_stat parameter to shutil.copytree():
      set it to false to skip copying permissions and times of
      directories with shutil.copystat(), e.g. when copying a
      read-only tree.
    - gh-159875: Fix AttributeError from the methods of an
      asyncio SSL transport, such as write() and set_protocol(),
      when the transport is closed after its connection was lost.
      This also affected the fallback of loop.sendfile() over SSL
      when the peer went away mid-transfer. The SSL context is
      still released once the connection is lost.
    - gh-160125: Support setting breakpoints with the pdb break
      and tbreak commands using package.module.function names
      when the module has not been imported in the current
      namespace.
    - gh-138641: Ignore pdb.set_trace() when called directly at
      the pdb prompt.
    - gh-159868: Allow collections.UserString.startswith() and
      collections.UserString.endswith() to accept a UserString
      instance as the prefix or suffix argument.
    - gh-159864: Fix a crash in syslog.openlog() under the
      free-threaded build when sys.argv is modified concurrently.
    - gh-159690: Fix logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler
      permanently stopping rollover after a rollover failed or
      its backup file already existed, for example at a DST
      change.
    - gh-159739: Avoid undefined behavior when struct.pack_into()
      copies a bytearray into overlapping output.
    - gh-159739: Fix allocation error handling in the fallback
      implementation of getaddrinfo().
    - gh-159739: Fix a double free if remote unwinder
      initialization runs out of memory.
    - gh-159739: Fix io.IOBase.readline() returning more bytes
      than requested when a stream supports peek() and returns
      short reads.
    - gh-159739: Fix multibyte encoders silently consuming a
      non-BMP character when looking up a two-character mapping.
    - gh-159739: Improve performance when parsing email address
      groups with many members.
    - gh-159739: Fix off-by-one output buffer checks in the
      fallback implementation of getnameinfo().
    - gh-159739: Fix reference cycles involving the types of
      grapheme iterators and segments created by
      unicodedata.iter_graphemes().
    - gh-159811: Fix a crash in hashlib when the OpenSSL routine
      used by hash.update() or by hash object constructors fails
      on data larger than 2048 bytes. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-159811: Fix a crash in hmac when the OpenSSL routine
      used by hmac.HMAC.update() or by hmac.new() fails on data
      larger than 2048 bytes. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-159786: Fix the error handling of the HACL* routine used
      by hmac.new() and hmac.HMAC.update(). If the maximum input
      length of the underlying hash function is exceeded, an
      OverflowError is now raised on all builds, instead of
      crashing on DEBUG builds and being silently ignored
      otherwise. Code correctness. Realistically this can only
      happen at implausible sizes. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-159739: Fix copying collections.deque subclasses with a
      large maximum length.
    - gh-159739: Allow cyclic garbage collection to reclaim group
      records returned by grp.
    - gh-159739: Fix io.BytesIO reads into overlapping views of
      the same buffer.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash when memory allocation fails while
      creating a collections.OrderedDict items iterator.
    - gh-159739: Avoid reading past the end of an encoding name
      when the surrogatepass error handler receives a truncated
      UTF-16 or UTF-32 name.
    - gh-159739: Fix incorrect ctypes scalar values after
      ctypes.resize() enlarges the object.
    - gh-159739: Fix a memory leak when Unicode normalization
      cannot grow its temporary buffer.
    - gh-159739: Fix resource leaks in ssl when certificate
      conversion or key log setup fails.
    - gh-159706: Fix the pure-Python zoneinfo.ZoneInfo setting
      fold=0 in fromutc() for times in the fold created by the
      only transition of a zone with a single transition.
    - gh-71990: ctypes: objects with an _as_parameter_ attribute
      are now implicitly converted when passed for a POINTER()
      argument.
    - gh-139122: uuid.UUID now consistently raises TypeError when
      the bytes or bytes_le argument is not a bytes object.
      Previously, some invalid inputs raised AssertionError or
      ValueError.
    - gh-78327: ctypes data types now set __hash__() to None, so
      collections.abc.Hashable checks report them correctly.
    - gh-159714: Fix zoneinfo.ZoneInfo interpreting the Julian
      day rule J59 as February 29 in leap years instead of
      February 28.
    - gh-149015: Fix bdb.Bdb.clear_all_file_breaks() leaving
      breakpoints behind when multiple breakpoints are set on the
      same line.
    - gh-159684: Update configparser and its tests to modern
      linter standards: printf-style and str.format() call sites
      are now f-strings, and a handful of constructs have simpler
      spellings. No behavior change.
    - gh-159465: Preserve SyntaxError for malformed escapes in
      unfinished f-strings and t-strings passed to
      codeop.compile_command().
    - gh-155976: curses.set_term() and curses.screen.use() now
      update curses.LINES, curses.COLS, curses.COLORS and
      curses.COLOR_PAIRS for the current screen.
    - gh-157210: Fix entering a combining character in the
      lower-right cell of curses.textpad.Textbox: it no longer
      takes a cell of its own, pushing its base character off the
      window. In insert mode, a combining character no longer
      shifts the following text.
    - gh-159643: Fix EOFError raised by tarfile in stream mode
      with bz2, xz or zstd compression when reading past the end
      of the compressed data, for example with ignore_zeros or an
      archive without end-of-archive blocks.
    - gh-159620: Fix python -m asyncio ps, pstree and async-aware
      profiling.sampling stacks stopping at asynchronous
      generators. Patch by Timofei Ivankov.
    - gh-159558: Speed up assignment to the value attribute of
      simple ctypes types, to the contents attribute of ctypes
      pointers and to ctypes structure fields, array items and
      pointer items on the free-threaded build by not re-entering
      the critical section already held on the object.
    - gh-159435: Fix an offset calculation in tarfile when a PAX
      header with a size record is followed by a GNU long-name
      header. Such archives could duplicate or skip members while
      being read.
    - gh-159458: Fix a ThreadSanitizer data race on the static
      cache in normalize_century() of the datetime module under
      the free-threaded build.
    - gh-159503: Fix quadratic copying in asyncio selector socket
      transports on partial sends. A bytearray passed to write()
      now stays locked against resizing until it has been sent.
    - gh-159500: Speed up asyncio.StreamReader.readline() and
      asyncio.StreamReader.readuntil() when the data is already
      buffered, and stop readuntil() with a tuple of separators
      from scanning the whole buffer on every call.
    - gh-159465: Improve incomplete input detection in codeop
      without an extra parser pass, and preserve syntax and
      compiler errors.
    - gh-81954: Fix zipfile.ZipFile not being closed at
      interpreter shutdown when emitting its ResourceWarning
      failed with an ImportError.
    - gh-159430: Report the correct exception if looking up
      __name__ raises an exception when calling repr() on a
      weakref.ref.
    - gh-159387: Fix ssl reporting TLS 1.0, 1.1, and 1.2 as
      unavailable when built with OpenSSL 4.0, despite support
      for these protocol versions.
    - gh-159398: Fix the sampling profiler crashing when a string
      read from the target process contains code points above
      U+10FFFF.
    - gh-159322: Fix tarfile to NUL-terminate user and group
      names in PAX archive headers and use extended headers for
      names longer than 31 characters.
    - gh-159304: Fix AttributeError in
      email.message.EmailMessage.get_body() when a nested
      multipart part is malformed and its payload is a string.
    - gh-159225: Prevent input calls in PyREPL from modifying
      readline history.
    - gh-159240: Deprecate, and schedule for removal in Python
      3.20, the __author__, __credits__, __copyright__ and
      __date__ attributes of bz2, concurrent.futures, inspect,
      io, json, logging, optparse, platform, pydoc, tarfile,
      tkinter.ttk, tokenize and uuid.
    - gh-158501: datetime.time.fromisoformat() and
      datetime.datetime.fromisoformat() now reject stray text
      between the time and a UTC offset. The C implementation
      previously accepted strings that the pure-Python
      implementation rejected.
    - gh-72113: Speed up creating a ctypes array from
      initializers, such as (c_int * 3)(1, 2, 3), by roughly 3x.
    - gh-158856: Improve large Enum creation performance.
    - gh-159044: Restore the previous behaviour of
      http.client.HTTPConnection.set_tunnel() where header values
      that are not strings (such as None, int or other objects)
      are converted with str instead of raising AttributeError
      when the request is sent.
    - gh-159168: Fix RecursionError in python -m asyncio pstree
      on a deep chain of awaiting tasks. Patch by Timofei
      Ivankov.
    - gh-88037: urllib.parse.urlsplit() and
      urllib.parse.urlparse() now raise ValueError for an invalid
      port when the URL is parsed, instead of when the port
      attribute is read. Patch by Miguel Brito and Senthil
      Kumaran.
    - gh-159184: The output of marshal.dumps() no longer depends
      on the order of the elements of a set which have the same
      marshalled form, such as NaNs which are distinct objects.
    - gh-159049: Fix reference cycles in
      asyncio.loop.create_connection() and
      asyncio.loop.start_tls() after a failed TLS handshake.
      Patch by Timofei Ivankov.
    - gh-150751: http.client now ignores optional whitespace
      around the Content-Length header value when validating it,
      as required by RFC 9112. Previously a value with trailing
      whitespace (for example Content-Length: 5 followed by a
      space) was treated as missing and the response body was
      read until the connection was closed. (CVE-2026-103995,
      bsc#1288328)
    - gh-158998: Fix os.statx() ignoring the follow_symlinks
      argument.
    - gh-158628: Implement sys._wasi_info for exposing
      WASI-specific system details.
    - gh-158287: Fix a bug in asyncio where stopping a child
      process (such as with SIGSTOP) on macOS caused the event
      loop to block indefinitely.
    - gh-155233: Fix asyncio.Barrier.wait() returning duplicate
      indices when a waiting task is cancelled before the barrier
      is released.```
    - gh-158839: The log functions in the logging module and the
      logging.Logger class now normalize falsy exc_info arguments
      to None before passing them to logging.Logger.makeRecord()
      and subsequently to logging.LogRecord. This aligns
      logging.LogRecord.exc_info with the documentation.
    - gh-130698: Fix PyREPL to convert sys.ps1 and sys.ps2 to
      strings before use, and fall back to the default prompts if
      the conversion raises.
    - gh-158192: Expose the future being waited on by a
      FutureIter as fi_future.
    - gh-158370: concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter objects now
      support the context manager protocol.
    - gh-158277: Fix sqlite3 CLI completer to include view
      columns in column-name completion.
    - gh-144650: Use Argument Clinic vectorcall support for the
      decimal.Decimal type. This offers 1.10x speedup on creation
      of small instances.
    - gh-158159: Fix a use-after-free in asyncio.Task.get_name()
      when formatting the default task name triggers a garbage
      collection whose finalizers call get_name() on the same
      task.
    - gh-158126: Speed up pickle.dumps() and creating a
      pickle.Pickler by avoiding the creation of an
      AttributeError when looking up the optional
      reducer_override and dispatch_table attributes.
    - gh-158095: Fix a memory leak in re.finditer() and regular
      expression scanners when their input participates in a
      reference cycle.
    - gh-144812: Make argparse.ArgumentGroup and
      argparse.MutuallyExclusiveGroup public. The private
      _ArgumentGroup and _MutuallyExclusiveGroup names remain as
      aliases.
    - gh-158004: Fix asyncio.as_completed() to continue yielding
      every awaitable after a pending iteration step is
      cancelled.
    - gh-89977: Avoid releasing the GIL for
      socket.socket.setblocking(), socket.socket.getsockname(),
      socket.socket.getpeername(), and socket.gethostname().
    - gh-157928: Correctly detect and handle OSC sequences in
      PyREPL.
    - gh-157899: os.readlink() now accepts a file descriptor
      referring to a symlink on Linux, Android, macOS and iOS.
    - gh-157880: Fix mailbox.Babyl to write the visible headers
      of a mailbox.BabylMessage to the mailbox file.
    - gh-157856: Fix asyncio.as_completed() raising RuntimeError
      (“no running event loop”) when the iterator is created
      outside of a running event loop and driven with
      loop.run_until_complete().
    - gh-49960: ctypes callback functions can now return
      structures and unions by value. Previously only “simple”
      types could be returned, and any other result type raised
      TypeError.
    - gh-157290: Add the %Nf format code (where N is from 1 to 6)
      to datetime.datetime.strftime(), datetime.time.strftime(),
      datetime.date.strftime(), datetime.datetime.strptime() and
      datetime.time.strptime().
    - gh-158252: Speed up time.strptime(),
      datetime.date.strptime(), datetime.time.strptime(), and
      datetime.datetime.strptime() for common numeric formats by
      parsing fields and constructing the result in C. Other
      inputs continue to use the Python parser.
    - gh-160837: asyncio.print_call_graph() no longer truncates
      the call stack of a task suspended inside an asynchronous
      generator.
    - gh-156784: asyncio.ProactorEventLoop no longer silently
      ignores ConnectionResetError on UDP sockets, matching
      asyncio.SelectorEventLoop.
    - gh-156568: zipapp.create_archive() now correctly sets the
      executable bit on the target archive when copying a zipapp
      where the target is a path-like object.
    - gh-154675: Improve import time of pdb, bdb and code by
      lazily importing several dependencies.
    - gh-151126: Fix a crash caused by failing to set MemoryError
      on allocation failure when first using a Chinese, Japanese
      or Korean codec.
    - gh-156057: Wrap the underlying compression library’s
      exception in tarfile.ReadError when a member’s compressed
      data is corrupt past its header, for all of tarfile’s
      supported compression formats (gzip, bzip2, lzma, zstd).
      Previously the raw exception (e.g. zlib.error) could leak
      through tarfile.TarFile.extractfile(). Patch by Jason Mak.
    - gh-156078: zipfile.ZipFile.mkdir() now raises ValueError
      when the archive is closed or when a writable member handle
      is open.
    - gh-155833: Ensure that MD5 and SHA* objects are properly
      GC-untracked before freeing their internal HACL* state.
      Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-155830: _blake2: Ensure that BLAKE-2 objects are
      correctly initialized before being tracked by the garbage
      collector. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-155782: ssl: prevent a crash in group() for session-less
      objects on OpenSSL 3.2 and later. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-155428: Ensure that hmac.digest() and hmac.HMAC.digest()
      output identical values when using a digest’s block size
      smaller than 16. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-155426: Make sure that the pure Python fallback of
      hmac.digest() reject keys that are neither bytes or
      bytearray. Previously, an AttributeError was raised instead
      of TypeError. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-153711: On iOS, add os.pipe2(), and use the syscalls
      pipe2 (2) and dup3 (2) internally, when available at both
      build-time and run-time.
    - gh-155152: Improve performance of some zipimport archives
      that use Zstandard compression.
    - gh-148228: The REPL now displays error messages when
      editing commands cannot be performed, such as when tab
      completion finds no matches or a history search fails.
      Patch by Bartosz Sławecki.
    - gh-74876: Weak references (weakref.ref),
      weakref.WeakMethod, weakref.WeakSet,
      weakref.WeakValueDictionary and weakref.WeakKeyDictionary
      can now be pickled if the weakly referenced objects are
      strongly referenced elsewhere in the same pickle; otherwise
      pickling raises pickle.PicklingError. weakref.WeakMethod
      and weakref.WeakSet can now also be copied.
    - gh-153679: zipimport.zipimporter now raises
      zipimport.ZipImportError instead of UnicodeDecodeError for
      a UTF-8-flagged file name that is not valid UTF-8. Patch by
      tonghuaroot.
    - gh-153605: Fix gettext.GNUTranslations raising struct.error
      instead of OSError when reading a malformed .mo file. Patch
      by tonghuaroot.
    - gh-149816: hashlib: fix a crash arising from a race
      condition when looking up an OpenSSL hash algorithm by name
      the first time. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-62222: Fix binascii.a2b_qp() and quopri discarding the
      character after a = that does not start a valid escape:
      b'==41' now decodes to b'=A', as in the email package. Add
      a keyword-only strip_ws parameter to binascii.a2b_qp(),
      quopri.decode() and quopri.decodestring() to strip trailing
      whitespace from each line, as required by RFC 2045.
    - gh-152490: Fix TypeError when formatting a SyntaxError
      raised with NotImplemented as its argument, which caused
      unexpected REPL exit and IDLE Shell restart.
    - gh-152373: Fix the pdb until command not stepping over a
      list comprehension when a breakpoint is set on it. Patch by
      tonghuaroot.
    - gh-151633: Fix a use-after-free under free-threading when
      multiple threads update the same Counter concurrently.
    - gh-105578: Deprecate typing.AnyStr type variable and raise
      a warning when it is imported.
    - gh-149527: multiprocessing: fix creation of temporary
      socket files following gh-137335 (PR#148578 and
      corresponding backports). Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-149309: bdb.BdbQuit is now a subclass of BaseException,
      instead of Exception, to allow it to be used for cleanly
      exiting the debugger without being accidentally caught by
      user code.
    - gh-149083: functools.Placeholder is now a sentinel. It is
      no longer an instance of its own singleton type.
    - gh-143376: concurrent.interpreters: fix a crash when
      internal cross-interpreter channel ends have incorrect
      channel IDs. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-146169: xml.parsers.expat: raise RuntimeError when an
      Expat handler calls parser.Parse or parser.ParseFile on the
      parser that called the handler. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-146065: Fix a crash in asyncio.Future iterator when
      send() is called after throw() or close().
    - gh-84644: Deprecate using a return annotation to infer the
      dispatch type for functools.singledispatch() and
      functools.singledispatchmethod. It will raise TypeError in
      Python 3.21. Annotate the dispatch parameter or pass the
      dispatch type explicitly instead. Patch by Bartosz
      Sławecki.
    - gh-84027: shutil now can unpack wheel packages using the
      whl format.
    - gh-140036: Avoid hanging in floor division of pure Python
      decimal.Decimal instances when the context precision is
      very large. Patch by Bénédikt Tran.
    - gh-139105: Correct the EOF key shown in the sqlite3 CLI
      .help text on Windows.
    - gh-139122: uuid: Reimplement UUID objects, uuid4(), and
      uuid7() in C.
    - gh-89730: Add support for Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) to
      the ssl module with OpenSSL 4.0 or later.
    - gh-115810: Add datetime.timezone.name, the name passed to
      the constructor, or None if no name was passed.
    - gh-129605: Improve exception handling when computing
      suggestions in traceback.py. This fixes a bug that could
      cause PyREPL to exit unexpectedly.
    - gh-128289: Add eager_tasks parameter to asyncio.run()
      function and asyncio.Runner class constructor.
    - gh-61448: Fix inspect.formatargvalues() raising KeyError
      for deleted arguments, including *args and **kwargs, by
      displaying <deleted>. Patch by Ezio Melotti and Furkan
      Onder.
    - bpo-19094: The urllib.parse URL parsing functions now raise
      TypeError instead of AttributeError when passed an object
      which is not a string, bytes, or None. Accepting objects
      with false values (like 0 and []) except empty strings,
      byte-like objects and None is now deprecated, extending the
      deprecation made in Python 3.14 for parse_qsl() and
      parse_qs().
    - bpo-44170: Fix UnicodeDecodeError with multibyte utf8
      characters in ShareableList.
  - Documentation
    - gh-138277: Rearranged documentation search results to
      emphasize built-in types and functions. Patch by Adam
      Hartz.
    - gh-107689: Added docstrings to abstract ctypes.
  - Tests
    - gh-160334: Fix the sampling profiler integration test for
      special frames without file and line information.
    - gh-161517: Fix test_gdb when Python is built out-of-tree
      and Python is run from a virtual environment. Previously,
      test_gdb was just skipped. Patch by Victor Stinner.
    - gh-161430: No longer list tests expected to be skipped in
      the final report. Patch by Victor Stinner.
    - gh-161263: Skip tests which use MD5 algorithm for
      WWW-Authenticate challenges when libssl is in FIPS mode.
    - gh-158646: Fix a race in test_asyncio.test_sslproto where
      the server side of
      test_shutdown_corrupted_ssl_sends_close_notify could fail
      with a connection reset on Windows.
    - gh-107862: Add hypothesis.stateful and the timezones() and
      ip_addresses() strategies to the Hypothesis stubs used when
      Hypothesis is not installed.
    - gh-159293: Restore the recursion limit after the
      free-threading recursion-limit race test to avoid failures
      in subsequent tests run in the same process.
    - gh-158975: Replace fixed sleeps used for synchronization in
      multiprocessing tests with bounded waits to avoid failures
      on slow or overloaded systems. Ensure pool cleanup runs
      even when assertions fail in the imap buffer tests.
    - gh-158895: When run in GitHub Actions, test.regrtest now
      annotates each test failure in the job log and writes a
      summary of the failures to the job summary.
  - Build
    - gh-161467: Enable the use of __attribute__((hot)) when
      building CPython with Clang and other compilers that
      support it.
    - gh-160924: Fix cross-compilation failures with
      --enable-shared caused by the build Python loading the
      target’s libpython through the shared-library search path
      (such as musl from glibc).
    - gh-75929: Fix a configure probe that could omit functions
      such as os.fchdir() from builds using -Wall -Werror.
    - gh-160704: Fix C11-C17 builds with old C library headers
      that do not define static_assert, including glibc versions
      older than 2.16.
    - gh-160689: The build helper programs
      Programs/_freeze_module and _bootstrap_python are now
      linked only with the modules of Modules/Setup.bootstrap,
      instead of with every static module. Builtin modules added
      via Modules/Setup.local or MODULE_BUILDTYPE=static can now
      depend on frozen modules or on getpath.
    - gh-128884: Report a configuration error when --enable-bolt
      is used with build flags that explicitly request the
      Cortex-A53 erratum 843419 workaround. Document how to
      disable the workaround for builds that will not run on
      affected processors.
    - gh-128883: Fix crashes with -X perf and -X perf_jit in BOLT
      builds. The ELF perf trampoline templates now use read-only
      data sections.
    - gh-128884: Fix --enable-bolt build failures on AArch64 with
      recent LLVM: pass -frame-opt=hot only on x86. Patch by
      Donghee Na.
    - gh-160004: Fix the paths in the PEP 739 build-details.json
      file generated by Tools/build/generate-build-details.py
      with both --relative-paths and --config-file-path.
      Previously, every path except base_prefix was wrong and
      depended on the directory the script was run from.
    - gh-159998: Fix libpython.dynamic in the PEP 739
      build-details.json file for macOS and iOS framework builds.
      It now points at the framework’s library instead of a
      nonexistent path under lib/.
    - gh-144942: Fix the macOS shared library and framework
      builds not linking the libraries required by built-in
      modules, such as the HACL* objects needed by _blake2 when
      it is built in via Modules/Setup.local.
    - gh-143632: Fix the check that disables PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME
      on musl libc: it tested an unset variable, so it never had
      any effect and the build could fail with a redefinition of
      struct prctl_mm_map.
    - gh-131999: Platform support for Apple’s tvOS, watchOS and
      visionOS was added.
    - gh-153195: The PEG parser generator now supports splitting
      a grammar into several files with the @include meta, and
      generates a separate C file for the rules of each included
      file. The rules for specialized syntax errors moved from
      Grammar/python.gram to Grammar/invalid.gram, which
      generates the new Parser/parser_invalid.c.
    - gh-159819: Fix the shell version of python3-config (used on
      all POSIX platforms except macOS) when the installation
      prefix contains spaces or other characters special to the
      shell or sed: it printed an empty --prefix and wrong
      --includes/--ldflags paths while exiting successfully. The
      script now also exits with status 1 if it cannot determine
      its installation prefix.
    - gh-54767: The --enable-loadable-sqlite-extensions=no and
      --disable-loadable-sqlite-extensions configure options now
      disable loadable SQLite extensions instead of enabling
      them.
    - gh-159759: Fix the libpython.static path in PEP 739
      build-details.json, which pointed to a file that is not
      installed when building with --enable-shared, and no longer
      list a static library for framework builds, which do not
      install one.
    - gh-75382: Make configure fail early with a clear error when
      a --with-*-sanitizer option is used but a program cannot be
      linked with the corresponding -fsanitize flag, for example
      because the sanitizer runtime library is not installed.
    - gh-159452: Tools/build/regen-configure.sh no longer leaves
      root-owned files in the source tree.
    - gh-159440: The version string reported by sys.version no
      longer carries a spurious -dirty suffix when CPython is
      built out-of-tree from a clean git checkout: the build
      stamp now checks the source tree instead of the build
      directory.
    - gh-157949: Remove dead build and preprocessor code for SCO
      UnixWare, OpenUNIX, SCO OpenServer and ReliantUNIX.
    - gh-157354: Fix the --with-name-sanitizer=no and
      --without-name-sanitizer configure options enabling the
      sanitizer instead of disabling it.
    - gh-156780: Emscripten libpython.a can now be linked into a
      program statically.
    - gh-155813: On macOS, LIBFFI_CFLAGS and LIBFFI_LIBS are no
      longer ignored when the SDK provides libffi, so ctypes can
      again be built against a different libffi. Patch by Advit
      Arora.
    - gh-153285: Fix incorrect executable linking on macOS with
      --with-lto caused by premature expansion of Make’s $@
      target variable.
  - Windows
    - gh-160239: Remove dead and broken _repr_info() methods from
      asyncio.windows_events; they called Future._repr_info(),
      which no longer exists.
    - gh-159880: Fix a key handle leak in winreg.CreateKey(),
      winreg.CreateKeyEx() and winreg.OpenKey() when the
      winreg.OpenKey/result audit hook fails.
    - gh-159118: Fix a crash (RPC_NT_INTERNAL_ERROR) and
      intermittent window class failures in _wmi under high
      concurrency and load by initializing COM as multi-threaded
      (MTA) instead of apartment-threaded (STA).
    - gh-157418: Correct the third parameter name of
      IocpProactor.recvfrom_into() from flags to nbytes to
      reflect that it specifies the number of bytes to receive.
  - macOS
    - gh-159739: Propagate errors that occur while converting
      macOS system proxy settings.
  - WASI
    - gh-161367: Add a test command to Platforms/WASI with
      --fast-ci and --slow-ci to select fast CI or slow Buildbot
      tests and --target to test the build, gathered
      distribution, or release archive.
    - gh-160135: Support wasm32-wasip3.
  - IDLE
    - gh-161477: Fix repr() of
      idlelib.redirector.WidgetRedirector and
      idlelib.redirector.OriginalCommand, which displayed a
      spurious one-element tuple.
    - gh-159517: Fix the completion list and the call tip
      grabbing the focus on macOS with Tcl/Tk 9.1.
  - Tools/Demos
    - gh-87613: Extend Argument Clinic The Vectorcall Protocol to
      support Heap Types with zero argument construction.
    - gh-114258: Argument Clinic now supports the __next__ type
      slot (tp_iternext), including @critical_section.
    - gh-159385: iOS builds can now be configured to generate
      free-threading or debug output.
    - gh-131725: Tools/i18n/msgfmt.py now writes a hash table to
      the generated .mo file, as GNU msgfmt does.
  - C API
    - gh-160109: Remove the unused FVS_MASK and FVS_HAVE_SPEC
      macros. They were used by the FORMAT_VALUE opcode, which
      was removed in Python 3.13.
    - gh-161407: Fix a crash at exit when an audit hook was added
      with PySys_AddAuditHook() before Py_Initialize() and the
      raw memory allocator changed during startup, for example
      with PYTHONMALLOC=mimalloc or in the Python Development
      Mode.
    - gh-160962: Fix PyInitConfig_SetStr() when setting an
      optional string option to NULL. Previously, the function
      crashed. Patch by Victor Stinner.
    - gh-161226: _PyTuple_Resize() now fails with SystemError if
      the hash value was already computed. Patch by Victor
      Stinner.
    - gh-161185: Fix a strict aliasing issue in the memcpy()
      implementation of Py_SETREF, Py_XSETREF and Py_CLEAR
      macros. Patch by Nathan Goldbaum and Victor Stinner.
    - gh-161172: Add the PyUnicodeWriter API to the limited C
      API. Patch by Victor Stinner.
    - gh-159739: Avoid a crash if a context watcher is cleared
      while other context watchers are being notified.
    - gh-159739: Fix a crash in _PyTuple_Resize() when resizing a
      non-empty tuple to a negative or too large size. It now
      raises SystemError or MemoryError respectively.
    - gh-159739: PyInitConfig_SetStr() now releases a previously
      configured value and preserves it if conversion of the
      replacement fails.
    - gh-159739: Fix a reference leak when _PyTuple_Resize()
      fails.
    - gh-157384: PyImport_CreateModuleFromInitfunc() now accepts
      non-ASCII module names for multi-phase init modules,
      instead of raising UnicodeEncodeError.
    - gh-156133: Add PyUnstable_InterpreterFrame_GetLocal() to
      read a local variable of an internal interpreter frame by
      its localsplus index, and
      PyUnstable_Code_GetLocalPlusNames() to get the matching
      variable names.
    - gh-153410: Add PyDict_AsFrozenDictAndClear() C-API function
      to create frozendict from existing dict object and clear
      the input dict instance.

